 real cache growth/reclaim, Pressure and bounded Query/replay. These are functional tests, not recall-quality tests.
 
+For managed KVMem requests, elastic mode trims unused KV on the first shorter request after prefix/session
+admission. It retains every row of the accepted resident view and room for the current request, rather than
+the previous request's high water. Parked sessions retain their Host-backed history. KV still grows in 4096-row
+steps with 1024 rows of lookahead. `poly_elastic_test MODEL.gguf --kv-reclaim-test` checks accepted KV, recurrent
+state, statistics and restored-session logits across immediate reclamation.
+
